.TH TGKILL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
tgkill \- Linux x86-64 syscall 234
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int tgkill(pid_t process, pid_t thread, int signal);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sends a signal to a specific thread in a thread group.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tgkill (2)
